From $26,760 to $45,370 the rate is 29%, higher than the 20.5% before it. BC tax starts here, and the BC tax reduction, which lowers your BC tax, shrinks by 3.56 cents for every dollar of income above $25,570. So more of each extra dollar goes to BC tax. The reduction is gone at about $45,370 of salary.
Once the reduction is gone, the rate falls to 25.5%. It is 28% from $50,840 (the next BC bracket) and 34% from $59,080 (the federal 20.5% bracket).
Then it falls as Employment Insurance and the Canada Pension Plan stop: 33% at $68,900, 31% at $74,600 and 28% at $85,000. After that it climbs to a top rate of 53.5%, where the line is straight.
From $266,680 of salary the line is straight: the rate stops rising, and every extra dollar loses the top rate, 53.5%.

yearTotal
